265
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,350
It pushes giant Jito aside.

266
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:16,060
It goes directly toward Japan's goal.

267
00:16:20,070 --> 00:16:22,530
He- He stopped it!

268
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:25,280
- What!?
- Wa- Wakabayashi!

269
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:27,910
Great catch, Wakabayashi.

270
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:35,160
Japan's goalkeeper Wakabayashi managed to catch Schneider's Fire Shot.

271
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:37,130
For the first time in this tournament!

272
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:38,710
What an incredible move.

273
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:42,420
Japan's super famous goalkeeper, Genzo Wakabayashi!

274
00:16:42,670 --> 00:16:45,680
This is the Wakabayashi I know. Great save!

275
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,390
Your work was perfect, Wakabayashi.

276
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:57,310
This gesture by Schneider means he will score next time.

277
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,650
Until now, Japan has dominated the midfield...

278
00:17:00,730 --> 00:17:05,530
But if Schneider moves to midfield, things will get a bit chaotic.

279
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:08,320
I will score next time.

280
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:12,830
I swear I will show my family a goal.

281
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,790
Germany will score the first goal.

282
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:18,670
That determination...

283
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,080
It reminds me.

284
00:17:20,710 --> 00:17:24,340
Right. Two weeks ago in Hamburg.

285
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:28,590
If Schneider changes his position and plays in midfield...

286
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:31,600
Then I'll mark him.

287
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,520
Ozora Tsubasa.

288
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:39,690
Three years ago

289
00:17:35,730 --> 00:17:39,690
Wakabayashi used to talk about him with pride constantly.

290
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:43,400
Japan has one more great player.

291
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:54,080
Good. The defense was good!

292
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:57,460
You defended well! Soda, Matsuyama, you played great.

293
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:03,800
Jito, Ishizaki, you almost stopped him.

294
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,210
Oh, yeah.

295
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,010
But that shot was incredible!

296
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:11,840
I've never seen a shot like that in my life.

297
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:15,930
The ball didn't even touch me, my face got scratched from the air friction.

298
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:18,850
So this is Germany's famous Young Emperor.

299
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:21,060
Karl Heinz Schneider.

300
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:25,320
Dad, Mom, my brother almost scored.

301
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,570
Right.

302
00:18:26,650 --> 00:18:27,610
Yes.

303
00:18:31,570 --> 00:18:35,240
What a tremendous attack Schneider made from midfield.

304
00:18:35,330 --> 00:18:39,500
Will he change position and play in midfield?

305
00:18:39,710 --> 00:18:41,210
Schneider.

306
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,130
Are you going to be a midfielder?

307
00:18:43,630 --> 00:18:48,130
Wakabayashi is great and won't easily let me score.

308
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:52,470
Next time, I'll shoot from inside the penalty area.

309
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,430
For that, I want a pass in front of the goal.

310
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,020
Schneider.

311
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:58,600
Do you understand?

312
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:03,100
They have their Wakabayashi, our former teammate.

313
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:07,900
And everyone here has played against him a lot before in Germany.

314
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:12,910
They know all the information about us.

315
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:17,120
Schester. They knew.

316
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:20,410
You have a habit of dribbling from the left.

317
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,290
Otherwise, you wouldn't have lost the ball two times in a row.

318
00:19:26,210 --> 00:19:28,500
So that's what it was.

319
00:19:28,590 --> 00:19:30,670
Now I understand. It was Wakabayashi's work.

320
00:19:31,090 --> 00:19:34,680
Now that we know, we won't fall apart.

321
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:37,640
I leave the midfield to you, just pass to me.

322
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,720
Next time, I will definitely score.

323
00:19:39,810 --> 00:19:40,680
Okay.

324
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:44,810
Schneider is returning to the forward position.

325
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:47,190
He doesn't want to play in midfield.

326
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:51,240
So he wants to stay as a forward, not a midfielder.

327
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:57,910
The ball goes from Wakabayashi to Matsuyama.

328
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,120
Sawada!

329
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:02,540
And from there to midfielder Sawada.

330
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:04,580
Alright. I'll pass to Tsubasa-san.

331
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:09,840
So that's what it was. There's no need to be afraid anymore.

332
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:16,340
Oh, Schester tackles to get the ball.

333
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,720
Sawada falls down! And loses the ball.

334
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:23,730
Schester immediately gets up and starts dribbling.

335
00:20:23,850 --> 00:20:27,360
- Franz!
- Schester, advance!

336
00:20:27,690 --> 00:20:29,860
Misaki from Japan makes his move.

337
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:36,110
Good. Left.

338
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:42,370
Oh, Schester reads his hand and goes right, opposite to Misaki's direction.

339
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:48,840
The young gentleman of Germany's midfield, Franz Schester, is back.

340
00:20:49,130 --> 00:20:51,250
This time Tsubasa goes.

341
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:54,630
He went right, not Misaki's left.

342
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,640
I'll stop him.

343
00:21:03,770 --> 00:21:05,810
Kaltz dribbles.

344
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:09,270
He passes Sano and Sawada in an instant.

345
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:12,320
This is true European technique.

346
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,780
And this time, I'm playing seriously.

347
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,530
And he passes to Schneider in the penalty area.

348
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:20,660
This is the Hamburg synergy!

349
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:24,660
Hah. I will stop the pass to Schneider.

350
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:29,420
Oh, Kaltz made a mistake.

351
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,170
The ball goes in an unexpected direction.

352
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,420
No, it's not a mistake.

353
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:36,220
He wants you to think that, and then sends an accurate pass to a suitable spot.

354
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:38,800
This Hermann Kaltz is cunning.

355
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:41,390
Good.

356
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:42,930
What!?

357
00:21:43,350 --> 00:21:45,980
No, that wasn't a misplaced shot!

358
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:50,440
Germany's other forward, Margas, runs toward the pass.

359
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:51,810
This goal.

360
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:53,190
No!

361
00:21:54,150 --> 00:21:55,690
Catch!

362
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,700
Wakabayashi!

363
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:00,200
Wakabayashi!

364
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:01,950
Wakabayashi!

365
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:49,990
NEXT EPISODE
A FIERY FIRST NUMBER